From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:48:54 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] usb: dwc3: qcom: Set the VBUS override for the role being
 entered

dwc3_qcom_set_role_notifier() chooses the VBUS override from the role
that is being left: off when leaving the device role, on for every other
change. Going from host to "none", and from "none" to host, therefore
sets the override, so after a USB device is unplugged the controller is
told that a host supplies VBUS although nothing is attached.
dwc3_qcom_run_stop_notifier() also sets it whenever the gadget starts,
whatever the role.

Choose the override from the role being entered: on for the device
role, off otherwise, and set it on a gadget start only in the device
role. Peripheral-only controllers keep the device role and are not
affected.

The problem and the fix were described by Doctor Logix in the Perpetua
kernel (denialwm/linux-perpetua 4daa98a10ed7, "usb: dwc3: qcom: manage
runtime power from connector roles"); this is a re-implementation of
that part only. The runtime PM reference that commit holds in the
device role is not part of it.

Fixes: 21188e8d6d75 ("usb: dwc3: qcom: Implement glue callbacks to facilitate runtime suspend")
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c | 17 ++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
index fddad078a214..3fab555ecee4 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
@@ -737,19 +737,21 @@ static void dwc3_qcom_set_role_notifier(struct dwc3 *dwc, enum usb_role next_rol
 		return;
 	}
 
-	if (qcom->current_role == USB_ROLE_DEVICE)
-		dwc3_qcom_vbus_override_enable(qcom, false);
-	else if (qcom->current_role != USB_ROLE_DEVICE)
-		dwc3_qcom_vbus_override_enable(qcom, true);
+	/*
+	 * The override tells the controller that a host supplies VBUS, so it
+	 * belongs to the device role only: leaving host mode for "none" must
+	 * not leave it set.
+	 */
+	dwc3_qcom_vbus_override_enable(qcom, next_role == USB_ROLE_DEVICE);
 
 	pm_runtime_mark_last_busy(qcom->dev);
 	pm_runtime_put_sync(qcom->dev);
 
 	/*
 	 * Current role changes via usb_role_switch_set_role callback protected
-	 * internally by mutex lock.
+	 * internally by mutex lock. The gadget restart path reads it locklessly.
 	 */
-	qcom->current_role = next_role;
+	WRITE_ONCE(qcom->current_role, next_role);
 }
 
 static void dwc3_qcom_run_stop_notifier(struct dwc3 *dwc, bool is_on)
@@ -765,7 +767,8 @@ static void dwc3_qcom_run_stop_notifier(struct dwc3 *dwc, bool is_on)
 	if (!is_on)
 		return;
 
-	dwc3_qcom_vbus_override_enable(qcom, true);
+	/* A gadget that starts while no host is attached gets no VBUS either. */
+	dwc3_qcom_vbus_override_enable(qcom, READ_ONCE(qcom->current_role) == USB_ROLE_DEVICE);
 	pm_runtime_mark_last_busy(qcom->dev);
 }
 
